cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this research artifact, its method, or its measured results,
  please cite it using these metadata.
title: >-
  CircuitSage V2: Behaviour-Signature Fault Localization is Bounded by
  Structural Fault Equivalence
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered study of whether learned models can localize single stuck-at
  faults across unseen VLSI circuits. Six learned formulations were registered
  in advance and falsified; a method with zero learned parameters outperformed
  the best of them by roughly 182x on mean reciprocal rank. Subsequent analysis
  proved within-collision-set localization is not identifiable under a uniform
  fault prior, and that between 83.3 and 99.8 percent of ambiguous candidate
  sets are structurally equivalent - establishing that behaviour-signature
  localization resolves faults to their equivalence class, the finest resolution
  any response-based method can achieve. A falsifiable prediction frozen before
  a sealed test circuit was opened was subsequently confirmed. The
  pre-registered acceptance outcome is NOT MET, by capture infeasibility on the
  second independent test circuit rather than by a measured shortfall. This
  repository publishes the method, the pre-registered contracts, the
  hash-anchored audit trail, and the negative results.
